{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Implemented and pushed — Gerrit change 2652\n\nCommit `2d889f40c237` on `bug-337e-browser-tier-optout`, base `e510c64dbcb6`.\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2652\n\n### Evidence\n\n**AC3 — RED without the marker (the anti-vacuity criterion).** Demonstrated twice, at both\nlevels, with Chromium made unreachable (`PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH` pointed at an empty dir):\n\n- With `tests/e2e/browser-tier-optout.toml` present:\n  `pytest tests/e2e/test_editor_browser.py -q` -> `6 skipped, 1 warning`, each reason\n  `BROWSER TIER DELIBERATELY NOT RUN (local-only) - Chromium will not launch ... These\n  browser assertions did NOT execute; this is a recorded decision, not a pass. Why:\n  browser-tier-optout.toml (ticket 337e-b558-17a2-49bd).`\n- With the record MOVED AWAY, same command: `6 errors`, each\n  `Failed: BROWSER TIER SILENTLY SKIPPED - Chromium will not launch ... This tier did not\n  execute and nothing in the tree licenses that.` The unit suite goes from `12 passed` to\n  `3 failed`. Record restored afterwards.\n\n**AC4 — the summary distinguishes.** Under plain `-q` (no `-rs`), the warnings summary\ncarries the banner and the full recorded reasoning; a reader of a \"green\" run is told the\ntier did not run.\n\n**Local verification** (targeted; `make verify` deliberately not run per the load\nconstraint): `make lint` rc=0, `make typecheck` rc=0 (762 files),\n`check_mechanism_delta.py --check` `new=0 increased=0`, `check_complexity_baseline.py\n--check` `new=0 increased=0`, `pytest tests/e2e tests/unit/test_browser_tier_optout.py`\n`45 passed`, `pytest tests/unit -m repo_policy` `22 passed`, plus the six modules that\nreference `tests/e2e` `86 passed`. No baseline file edited; the only `.github/` path in the\ndiff is `_build-and-test.yml` (comment only).\n\n**Plan-review:** certified at `e510c64dbcb681fd8e14050a854dfce86f488faf`, after two BLOCK\niterations (G1G2/G6 on the two unenumerated in-module fixtures, then P4 on description\nlength). Both remediated, not forced.\n\nNot closed and not submitted: awaiting `LLM-Review` and `Verified`.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788574151444739020,"uuid":"c175e4c6-e68c-420a-95cb-04f017786735"}